Package: LICT
Type: Package
Title: Large Language Model-Based Identifier for Cell Types
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(person("Wenjin", "Ye", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "yewj27@mail2.sysu.edu.cn"),
             person("Yuanchen", "Ma", role = "aut", email = "maych25@mail.sysu.edu.cn"))
Description: Annotates cell types in single-cell RNA-sequencing data by asking
    several large language models (OpenAI GPT, Anthropic Claude, Google Gemini,
    Baidu ERNIE and Llama 3) to name the cell type behind each cluster's marker
    genes. Annotation reliability is then assessed with a talk-to-machine
    validation and feedback strategy.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
LazyData: true
Imports:
    dplyr,
    magrittr,
    reticulate,
    roxygen2,
    stringr
RoxygenNote: 7.3.1
Suggests:
    knitr,
    rmarkdown
VignetteBuilder: knitr
SystemRequirements: Python (>= 3.9) with the 'openai' module for the GPT
    provider; 'anthropic', 'google-genai' and 'requests' are required by the
    Claude, Gemini and ERNIE/Llama providers respectively
